+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+With `transport.history.enabled`, a client may ask for its own conversation metadata by sending `list_conversations`. The frame has no user id: the server uses the authenticated user on the connection, even if the JSON carries an extra `userId`. It is valid independently of whether history is enabled. `limit` is optional and must be an integer from 1 through 200. `before` is an optional cursor with both `updatedAt` (an ISO date string) and `sessionId` (a string); a malformed limit or cursor receives `INVALID_MESSAGE`. ([validated by: validates the list frame and its complete paging cursor before dispatch](../../src/transport/conversationHistory.acceptance.test.ts#L94))
+
+| Field              | Type   | Required | Description                                     |
+| ------------------ | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`             | string | Yes      | `"list_conversations"`                          |
+| `limit`            | number | No       | Maximum summaries, from 1 through 200           |
+| `before.updatedAt` | string | No       | ISO activity time of the last row already shown |
+| `before.sessionId` | string | No       | Session id of that same row                     |
+
+The request runs outside the per-session turn lock, so a streaming answer does not delay it. ([validated by: answers a list while the same session’s user turn is still running](../../src/transport/conversationHistory.acceptance.test.ts#L167))
 
